From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marc Lainez <marc.lainez@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:33:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] board: lenovo: add TB3-710F

U-Boot is packed as the kernel of an Android boot image in the boot
partition, loaded by LK at 0x80008000. The console is the framebuffer
LK leaves running.

Boot order: a Nerves disk image in userdata (its partition 1, the
active FAT boot slot, mapped with blkmap), then a Buildroot ext4 root
in userdata, then U-Boot fastboot. Both use extlinux.conf.

Fastboot over the MUSB gadget can only flash and erase "boot" (the
boot image region holding U-Boot) and "userdata" (up to the MTK BMT
pool). Holding Volume-Down at start, or "fastboot reboot-bootloader",
stays in fastboot; Volume-Up reboots into recovery.

LK boots recovery when the MT6323 RTC PDN1 recovery bit is set. U-Boot
sets it on entry and clears it right before starting Linux, so a hang
in U-Boot ends in a watchdog reset into recovery rather than a loop.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
